\fs96 \cf2 Control flow\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa400\partightenfactor0

\fs32 \cf2 Mojo includes several traditional control flow structures for conditional and repeated execution of code blocks.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa800\partightenfactor0

\fs64 \cf2 The 
\fs56 \cf10 \cb12 if
\fs64 \cf2 \cb1  statement\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0

\fs32 \cf2 Mojo supports the 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 if
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  statement for conditional code execution. With it you can conditionally execute an indented code block if a given {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://docs.modular.com/stable/mojo/manual/types/#booleans"}}{\fldrslt \cf5 \ul \ulc5 boolean}} expression evaluates to 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 True
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1 .\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\fs28 \cf13 \cb14 temp_celsius \cf5 =\cf13  Float64\cf5 (\cf15 25\cf5 )\cf13 \cb1 \
\cf5 \cb14 if\cf13  temp_celsius \cf5 >\cf13  \cf15 20\cf5 :\cf13 \cb1 \
\cb14     \cf5 print(\cf16 "It is warm."\cf5 )\cf13 \cb1 \
\cb14     \cf5 print(\cf16 "The temperature is"\cf5 ,\cf13  temp_celsius \cf5 *\cf13  \cf15 9\cf13  \cf5 /\cf13  \cf15 5\cf13  \cf5 +\cf13  \cf15 32\cf5 ,\cf13  \cf16 "Fahrenheit."\cf13  \cf5 )\cf13 \cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\qc\partightenfactor0

\fs32 \cf17 \
\pard\pardeftab720\qc\partightenfactor0
\cf18 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\fs28 \cf13 \cb14 It is warm.\cb1 \
\cb14 The temperature is 77.0 Fahrenheit.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0

\fs32 \cf2 You can write the entire 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 if
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  statement as a single line if all you need to execute conditionally is a single, short statement.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\fs28 \cf13 \cb14 temp_celsius \cf5 =\cf13  \cf15 22\cf13 \cb1 \
\cf5 \cb14 if\cf13  temp_celsius \cf5 <\cf13  \cf15 15\cf5 :\cf13  \cf5 print(\cf16 "It is cool."\cf5 )\cf13  \cf6 # Skipped because condition is False\cf13 \cb1 \
\cf5 \cb14 if\cf13  temp_celsius \cf5 >\cf13  \cf15 20\cf5 :\cf13  \cf5 print(\cf16 "It is warm."\cf5 )\cf13 \cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\qc\partightenfactor0

\fs32 \cf17 \
\pard\pardeftab720\qc\partightenfactor0
\cf18 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\fs28 \cf13 \cb14 It is warm.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0

\fs32 \cf2 Optionally, an 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 if
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  statement can include any number of additional 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 elif
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  clauses, each specifying a boolean condition and associated code block to execute if 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 True
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1 . The conditions are tested in the order given. When a condition evaluates to 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 True
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1 , the associated code block is executed and no further conditions are tested.\
Additionally, an 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 if
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  statement can include an optional 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 else
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  clause providing a code block to execute if all conditions evaluate to 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 False
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1 .\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\fs28 \cf13 \cb14 temp_celsius \cf5 =\cf13  \cf15 25\cf13 \cb1 \
\cf5 \cb14 if\cf13  temp_celsius \cf5 <=\cf13  \cf15 0\cf5 :\cf13 \cb1 \
\cb14     \cf5 print(\cf16 "It is freezing."\cf5 )\cf13 \cb1 \
\cf5 \cb14 elif\cf13  temp_celsius \cf5 <\cf13  \cf15 20\cf5 :\cf13 \cb1 \
\cb14     \cf5 print(\cf16 "It is cool."\cf5 )\cf13 \cb1 \
\cf5 \cb14 elif\cf13  temp_celsius \cf5 <\cf13  \cf15 30\cf5 :\cf13 \cb1 \
\cb14     \cf5 print(\cf16 "It is warm."\cf5 )\cf13 \cb1 \
\cf5 \cb14 else:\cf13 \cb1 \
\cb14     \cf5 print(\cf16 "It is hot."\cf5 )\cf13 \cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\qc\partightenfactor0

\fs32 \cf17 \
\pard\pardeftab720\qc\partightenfactor0
\cf18 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\fs28 \cf13 \cb14 It is warm.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

