\fs48 \cf2 Short-circuit evaluation\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0

\fs32 \cf2 Mojo follows {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Short-circuit_evaluation"}}{\fldrslt \cf5 \ul \ulc5 short-circuit evaluation}} semantics for boolean operators. If the first argument to an 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 or
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  operator evaluates to 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 True
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1 , the second argument is not evaluated.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\fs28 \cf5 \cb14 def\cf13  \cf21 true_func\cf5 ()\cf13  raises \cf5 ->\cf13  Bool\cf5 :\cf13 \cb1 \
\cb14     \cf5 print(\cf16 "Executing true_func"\cf5 )\cf13 \cb1 \
\cb14     \cf5 return\cf13  \cf15 True\cf13 \cb1 \
\
\cf5 \cb14 def\cf13  \cf21 false_func\cf5 ()\cf13  raises \cf5 ->\cf13  Bool\cf5 :\cf13 \cb1 \
\cb14     \cf5 print(\cf16 "Executing false_func"\cf5 )\cf13 \cb1 \
\cb14     \cf5 return\cf13  \cf15 False\cf13 \cb1 \
\
\cf5 \cb14 print(\cf16 'Short-circuit "or" evaluation'\cf5 )\cf13 \cb1 \
\cf5 \cb14 if\cf13  true_func\cf5 ()\cf13  \cf5 or\cf13  false_func\cf5 ():\cf13 \cb1 \
\cb14     \cf5 print(\cf16 "True result"\cf5 )\cf13 \cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\qc\partightenfactor0

\fs32 \cf17 \
\pard\pardeftab720\qc\partightenfactor0
